  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nFair weather, warming temperatures, and light to breezy afternoon\nwinds continue through the week as NV remains in between an \noffshore ridge, and a northern plains trough. Today through \nTuesday the ridge will build eastward over the west coast, this \nwill push the trough slowly eastward as well. This will cause \nheights to rise over Nevada, and the pressure gradient to relax \nsome allowing for the westerly afternoon winds to run at 10 MPH to\n20 MPH with a few gusts up to 30 MPH possible. The other notable \nchange will be the warm-up of temperatures this week into the \nnext. High temperatures look to warm from the low 80s to low 90s \nThursday, back into the upper 80s to upper 90s by next Wednesday. \nOvernight lows will also warm, rising back into the upper 40s to \nupper 50s by Sunday morning. Models are hinting at developing a \nshortwave upper trough somewhere over the NW US late Sunday into \nMonday of next week. Models are still wavering on the location of \nthis trough, with little to no run to run consistency in either \nthe GFS or ECMWF ensembles. Still even with the proximity of this \ntrough, both model suites keep NV dry while shifting winds out of \nthe north, and enhancing wind speeds to 15 to 25 MPH with gusts up\nto 40 MPH possible. across the northern tier of the silver state.\nThis will have to be watched for the potential for fire \nweather/wind headlines for the latter half of the weekend. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence for quiet, dry weather conditions with \nwarming temperatures lasting through next weekend.",
